## Backend Enhancement

### [MODIFY] `services/admin/analytics_service.py`

Replace the single `get_platform_overview()` with an enriched response:

```python
def get_platform_overview(self) -> dict:
    return {
        "kpis": self._kpis(),
        "revenue_trend": self._revenue_trend_30d(),
        "recent_signups": self._recent_signups(limit=8),
        "recent_payments": self._recent_payments(limit=8),
        "recent_groups": self._recent_groups(limit=6),
        "subscription_breakdown": self._subscription_breakdown(),
        "feedback_summary": self._feedback_summary(),
    }
```

**`_kpis()` — 6 KPI cards:**
| Key | Source | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `total_treasurers` | `COUNT(users WHERE role='treasurer')` | All-time signups |
| `active_treasurers` | `COUNT(users WHERE is_active=True AND role='treasurer')` | Currently active |
| `total_revenue_kes` | `SUM(subscription_payments.amount WHERE status='success')` | All-time revenue |
| `active_subscriptions` | `COUNT(subscriptions WHERE status='active')` | Active subscribers |
| `pending_tickets` | `COUNT(support_tickets WHERE status='open')` | Open support queue |
| `ai_accuracy_rate` | Heuristic (existing logic) | Parser accuracy |

**`_revenue_trend_30d()` — daily revenue for past 30 days:**
```python
# Groups subscription_payments by date, returns array of {date, amount}
# Used to render a sparkline / bar chart
```
Returns: `[{"date": "2026-08-01", "amount": 12000}, ...]` — 30 items

**`_recent_signups(limit=8)` — latest treasurer registrations:**
Returns: `[{"user_id", "name", "email", "is_active", "created_at"}]`

**`_recent_payments(limit=8)` — latest subscription payments:**
Joins `SubscriptionPayment` + `User` + `Plan`.
Returns: `[{"payment_id", "user_name", "plan_name", "amount", "currency", "method", "status", "created_at"}]`

**`_recent_groups(limit=6)` — latest groups created:**
Joins `Group` + `User`.
Returns: `[{"group_id", "group_name", "owner_name", "status", "created_at"}]`

**`_subscription_breakdown()` — plan distribution:**
Groups active subscriptions by `plan.name`.
Returns: `[{"plan": "Professional", "count": 45}, ...]`

**`_feedback_summary()` — feedback counts by status:**
Groups `app_feedback` by `status`.
Returns: `{"new": 12, "reviewing": 3, "planned": 5, "shipped": 2, "declined": 1}`

